  "description": "CUVMIR crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C88 H91 Dy3 Fe6 N14 O50,3(C2 H3 N1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Fe1 (Fe) has 5 O neighbors; Fe2 (Fe) has 6 O neighbors; Fe3 (Fe) has 5 O neighbors; Fe4 (Fe) has 5 O neighbors; Fe5 (Fe) has 5 O neighbors; Fe6 (Fe) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 21 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 2.989-4.017 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 91.91-142.94°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Fe6IIIDy3III(μ4-O)3(μ3-O)(mdea)5(m-NO2C6H4COO)9]·3MeCN. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 3 μ4-O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 μ3-O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 3 μ4-O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 1 μ3-O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
